<div class="proof"><div class="shell">
  <div class="pcell rv">
    <div class="n"><span class="countup" data-count="36">0</span>%</div>
    <div class="c"><b>Highest score increase</b> achieved by a student on the Moretti Method</div>
  </div>
  <div class="pcell rv d1">
    <div class="n"><span class="countup" data-count="1500">0</span><small>+</small></div>
    <div class="c"><b>SAT scores for high-reaching students</b> &mdash; hundreds of points up from where they started</div>
  </div>
  <div class="pcell rv d2">
    <div class="n">+<span class="countup" data-count="200">0</span></div>
    <div class="c"><b>Largest single-section gain</b> on record, SAT Math</div>
  </div>
  <div class="pcell rv d3">
    <div class="n"><span class="countup" data-count="50">0</span><small>+</small></div>
    <div class="c"><b>Students supported</b> through course math, testing and applications over 8+ years</div>
  </div>
</div></div>

<section id="diagnostic"><div class="shell">
  <div class="shead rv">
    <div class="lbl">The diagnostic</div>
    <h2>Every program begins with a real test.</h2>
    <p>A full-length, timed, adaptive SAT taken at home. What comes back is not a score &mdash; it is a report that separates what your student doesn&rsquo;t know from what the clock took from them, because those need completely different fixes.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="dxscroll-wrap rv d1">
    <div class="dxscroll" id="dxscroll">

      <article class="dxpanel">
        <div class="pk">Path to target score</div>
        <h3>Where the next 110 points are.</h3>
        <p class="pcap">Every point between today&rsquo;s score and the target, attributed to the skill that will produce it.</p>
        <div class="dxplot"><div id="cBridge"></div><div class="dxtip" id="tBridge"></div></div>
        <div class="dxfootnote">Hover any step. Bars are the score; the floating blocks are what each block of work is worth.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="dxpanel">
        <div class="pk">What went wrong</div>
        <h3>One wrong answer, three fixes.</h3>
        <p class="pcap">Every miss sorted into what actually caused it &mdash; because re-teaching a skill will not fix a clock problem.</p>
        <div class="dxtoggle" role="group" aria-label="Choose section">
          <button type="button" data-sec="all" aria-pressed="true">Whole test</button>
          <button type="button" data-sec="math" aria-pressed="false">Math</button>
          <button type="button" data-sec="rw" aria-pressed="false">R&amp;W</button>
        </div>
        <div class="dxplot"><div id="cWrong"></div><div class="dxtip" id="tWrong"></div></div>
        <div class="dxlegend">
          <span><i style="background:#B0271C"></i>Didn&rsquo;t know it</span>
          <span><i style="background:#C9A84C"></i>Took too long</span>
          <span><i style="background:#4A4139"></i>Ran out of clock</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="dxpanel">
        <div class="pk">Where the time went</div>
        <h3>Pacing against the budget.</h3>
        <p class="pcap">Seconds per question on the first pass, and the extra time spent revisiting questions already answered.</p>
        <div class="dxplot"><div id="cPace"></div><div class="dxtip" id="tPace"></div></div>
        <div class="dxfootnote">The dashed line is the per-question budget. The lighter band is time spent on return trips &mdash; second-guessing, not solving.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="dxpanel">
        <div class="pk">Skills, ranked</div>
        <h3>Ordered by points recoverable.</h3>
        <p class="pcap">So week one starts on whatever moves the score most, rather than whatever comes first in a textbook.</p>
        <div class="dxplot"><div id="cSkills"></div><div class="dxtip" id="tSkills"></div></div>
        <div class="dxfootnote">Hatched bars appeared 1&ndash;4 times on this form &mdash; too few to judge, so they are neither flagged nor cleared. A second form settles them.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="dxpanel">
        <div class="pk">Habits worth naming</div>
        <h3>Accuracy against time spent.</h3>
        <p class="pcap">Each dot is one question. The quadrant it lands in says which habit is costing points.</p>
        <div class="dxplot"><div id="cQuad"></div><div class="dxtip" id="tQuad"></div></div>
        <div class="dxfootnote">Slow and wrong is a knowledge gap. Fast and wrong is carelessness. They need opposite interventions.</div>
      </article>

    </div>
    <div class="dxnav">
      <button type="button" id="dxPrev" aria-label="Previous chart"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 18l-6-6 6-6"/></svg></button>
      <button type="button" id="dxNext" aria-label="Next chart"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="dxread rv d2" style="margin-top:clamp(2rem,3.6vw,3rem)">
    <div class="dxr"><span class="dxi">1</span><div><h3>A range, not a guess</h3><p>Every score comes with the band it actually sits in. Precision you can trust beats a number that only sounds confident.</p></div></div>
    <div class="dxr"><span class="dxi">2</span><div><h3>Skills ranked by points recoverable</h3><p>So week one starts on the thing that moves the score most &mdash; not on whatever comes first in a textbook.</p></div></div>
    <div class="dxr"><span class="dxi">3</span><div><h3>Where the time actually went</h3><p>Question by question, including minutes spent revisiting questions already answered. Second-guessing is a habit, and it is faster to fix than a knowledge gap.</p></div></div>
    <div class="dxr"><span class="dxi">4</span><div><h3>Honest about small samples</h3><p>Skills seen only once or twice are flagged as unsettled rather than judged. A second sitting resolves them.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="programs"><div class="shell">
  <div class="shead rv">
    <div class="lbl">What we teach</div>
    <h2>Three programs. One method behind all of them.</h2>
    <p>A real diagnostic, an individualized plan, and a guarantee tied to the outcome &mdash; whether the goal is a score, a grade, or an acceptance.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="offers">
    <a class="offer rv d1" href="prep-course.html">
      <div class="ph phmark"><div class="gmark"><span class="gg" style="font-size:clamp(3.2rem,6vw,5.2rem)">SAT</span><span class="gs">the digital test</span></div></div>
      <div class="in">
        <div class="k">College Entrance Exams</div>
        <h3>The 12-Week SAT Program</h3>
        <p>Twelve weekly one-on-one sessions built from your student&rsquo;s diagnostic, with full-length timed testing, weekly office hours, and a written update to you every week.</p>
        <div class="cov">SAT &middot; PSAT &middot; AP &amp; IB exams &middot; test-day strategy</div>
        <span class="go">Explore the program &rarr;</span>
      </div>
    </a>
    <a class="offer rv d2" href="math-program.html">
      <div class="ph phmark"><div class="gmark"><span class="gg" style="font-size:clamp(4.4rem,8vw,7rem)">&#8747;</span><span class="gs">Algebra 1 &rarr; Multivariable</span></div></div>
      <div class="in">
        <div class="k">Mathematics</div>
        <h3>The Math Mastery Program</h3>
        <p>Not homework help. A diagnostic-driven curriculum built around your student&rsquo;s actual course and textbook, with support between sessions and a guarantee tied to the grade.</p>
        <div class="cov">Algebra 1 &middot; Geometry &middot; Algebra 2 &middot; Precalculus &middot; AP Calculus AB &amp; BC &middot; AP Statistics &middot; Multivariable Calculus &middot; IB Mathematics</div>
        <span class="go">Explore the program &rarr;</span>
      </div>
    </a>
    <a class="offer rv d3" href="applications.html">
      <div class="ph phmark"><div class="gmark"><span class="gg" style="font-size:clamp(3.2rem,6vw,5.2rem)">650</span><span class="gs">words, personal statement</span></div></div>
      <div class="in">
        <div class="k">College Admissions</div>
        <h3>Essays &amp; Applications</h3>
        <p>One-on-one coaching for the personal statement and every supplemental &mdash; brainstorming, structure, and real revision. Your student writes every word; we make sure every word earns its place.</p>
        <div class="cov">Personal statement &middot; supplementals for every school &middot; deadline tracking &middot; rolling enrollment</div>
        <span class="go">Explore the program &rarr;</span>
      </div>
    </a>
  </div>
</div></section>



<section id="testimonials" class="tsec"><div class="wide">
  <div class="shead rv">
    <div class="lbl">Testimonials</div>
